<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2020/08/apple-india.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="alignleft size-full wp-image-756076" />India has proposed extending tax breaks until 2041 for foreign companies that supply machinery to their contract manufacturers, handing a win to Apple as it <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/10/apple-makes-one-four-iphones-india/">expands iPhone production</a> in the country, <a href="https://www.reuters.com/business/retail-consumer/india-proposes-extending-tax-breaks-contract-manufacturing-boost-apple-2026-08-03/"><em>Reuters</em> reports</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Introduced in February, the exemption previously ran only until 2031, and Apple had <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/15/apple-lobbying-india-to-change-tax-law/">long since lobbied against being taxed</a> on the high-end iPhone machinery it owns in India. The draft bill still has to be passed by both houses of parliament.<div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/india/">India</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/03/india-moves-to-extend-apple-tax-break/">India Moves to Extend Tax Break Apple Lobbied For</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/india-moves-to-extend-tax-break-apple-lobbied-for.2486359/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>